es 7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6039ac1c-5457-5290-ac27-3bef1aa6a1c5" :answer/id #uuid "6039ac1c-5457-5290-ac27-3bef1aa6a1c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{6}\\times {7}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30c3751b-aa47-5f18-947b-22a337814d23" :answer/id #uuid "30c3751b-aa47-5f18-947b-22a337814d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5}^{6}\\times 7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e39c2a75-ee61-55a4-869d-3b74872c3050" :question/id #uuid "e39c2a75-ee61-55a4-869d-3b74872c3050" :question/math-academy-id "q-68445" :question/problem "$(-2)^{7}=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $-2=(-1)\\times 2.$\n\nTo raise the product of two numbers to the power of $7$, we can raise each number to the power of $7,$ and then multiply:\n\n$$\n(-2)^{7}={((-1)\\times 2)}^{7}=(-1)^{7}\\times {2}^{7}\n$$\n\nSince $-1$ raised to an odd power is $-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n(-1)^{7}\\times {2}^{7}=(-1)\\times {2}^{7}=-{2}^{7}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-863419e1-d8dc-5457-8b79-510ab7d534cb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-863419e1-d8dc-5457-8b79-510ab7d534cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "863419e1-d8dc-5457-8b79-510ab7d534cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a7e9c31d-2006-5f0c-a724-e1f109175257" :answer-field/choices ["answer-68ad4902-2995-5cd1-92bc-a5eec0f5639c" "answer-a7e9c31d-2006-5f0c-a724-e1f109175257" "answer-854a5449-be1a-554f-bfbe-004b1ed634cd" "answer-b193f3aa-3324-5f7b-9b44-969041415948" "answer-94825fbb-d867-5726-8c12-559497f7dd43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68ad4902-2995-5cd1-92bc-a5eec0f5639c" :answer/id #uuid "68ad4902-2995-5cd1-92bc-a5eec0f5639c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7e9c31d-2006-5f0c-a724-e1f109175257" :answer/id #uuid "a7e9c31d-2006-5f0c-a724-e1f109175257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{2}^{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-854a5449-be1a-554f-bfbe-004b1ed634cd" :answer/id #uuid "854a5449-be1a-554f-bfbe-004b1ed634cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b193f3aa-3324-5f7b-9b44-969041415948" :answer/id #uuid "b193f3aa-3324-5f7b-9b44-969041415948" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94825fbb-d867-5726-8c12-559497f7dd43" :answer/id #uuid "94825fbb-d867-5726-8c12-559497f7dd43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186130340 :tutorial/content "To raise the product of two numbers to a power, we can raise each number to that power, and then multiply. This is the **power of product rule for exponents**. \n\nTo demonstrate, let's simplify the expression $(5 \\times 3)^4$ by applying the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n(5\\times 3)^4=5^4\\times 3^4\n$$\n\n**Note:** The power of product rule for exponents is really just a quicker alternative to using repeated multiplication, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5\\times 3)^{4} & = \\\\ {{(5\\times 3)\\times (5\\times 3)\\times (5\\times 3)\\times (5\\times 3)}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ copies}} & = \\\\ {{(5\\times 5\\times 5\\times 5)}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ copies}}\\times {{(3\\times 3\\times 3\\times 3)}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ copies}} & = \\\\ {5}^{4}\\times {3}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129355 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078610 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2e46b72d-8394-58eb-a628-c7c43d6a0834"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078916 :question/problem "What is the coefficient of $y$ in the expression $\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3y}{4}+\\frac{11z}{8}?$" :question/worked-solution "The expression has three terms: \n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2},\\,-\\frac{3y}{4},\\,\\frac{11z}{8}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe only term with the variable $y$ is $-\\frac{3y}{4},$ so $-\\frac{3}{4}$ is the coefficient of $y.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186076274 :answer-field/correct 17592186076277 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078612 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e9e375f3-04e5-5e92-84aa-677faf38ae91"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e9e375f3-04e5-5e92-84aa-677faf38ae91" :question/id #uuid "e9e375f3-04e5-5e92-84aa-677faf38ae91" :question/math-academy-id "q-67059" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of $a$ in the expression $6x-2y-7z?$" :question/worked-solution "We can rewrite the expression $6x-2y-7z$ as\n\n$$\n6x-2y-7z+0,\n$$\n\nand we can replace $0$ with $0a$ to get\n\n$$\n6x-2y-7z+0a.\n$$\n\nWe see that the coefficient of $a$ is $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ec89f1b4-7246-58b6-b78e-5814d0d13e49"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ec89f1b4-7246-58b6-b78e-5814d0d13e49" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec89f1b4-7246-58b6-b78e-5814d0d13e49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8ac1096e-c1ec-5138-80ca-f8a49701458c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5fe20a50-b7a3-59fd-86d7-e3fdf07429c9" "answer-8ac1096e-c1ec-5138-80ca-f8a49701458c" "answer-5f26e716-5948-5421-bf61-bb04d45e2f23" "answer-291f869a-c46d-58d4-8cdf-867a6f38c27d" "answer-0697dad3-46f6-5d10-89fa-4c837a032b92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fe20a50-b7a3-59fd-86d7-e3fdf07429c9" :answer/id #uuid "5fe20a50-b7a3-59fd-86d7-e3fdf07429c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ac1096e-c1ec-5138-80ca-f8a49701458c" :answer/id #uuid "8ac1096e-c1ec-5138-80ca-f8a49701458c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f26e716-5948-5421-bf61-bb04d45e2f23" :answer/id #uuid "5f26e716-5948-5421-bf61-bb04d45e2f23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-291f869a-c46d-58d4-8cdf-867a6f38c27d" :answer/id #uuid "291f869a-c46d-58d4-8cdf-867a6f38c27d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0697dad3-46f6-5d10-89fa-4c837a032b92" :answer/id #uuid "0697dad3-46f6-5d10-89fa-4c837a032b92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2e46b72d-8394-58eb-a628-c7c43d6a0834" :question/id #uuid "2e46b72d-8394-58eb-a628-c7c43d6a0834" :question/math-academy-id "q-175333" :question/problem "The coefficient of $w$ in the expression  $\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{y}{2}+\\frac{4w}{7}$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The expression has three terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}\\,,\\,-\\frac{y}{2}\\,,\\,\\frac{4w}{7}\n$$\n\nThe only term with the variable $w$ is $\\frac{4w}{7},$ so $\\frac{4}{7}$ is the coefficient of $w.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-331590f2-60f5-540b-bbc5-f95dc66e46bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-331590f2-60f5-540b-bbc5-f95dc66e46bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "331590f2-60f5-540b-bbc5-f95dc66e46bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b2d5a746-cbe2-5c4e-8250-a72bbefe43f6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2d5a746-cbe2-5c4e-8250-a72bbefe43f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2d5a746-cbe2-5c4e-8250-a72bbefe43f6" :answer/id #uuid "b2d5a746-cbe2-5c4e-8250-a72bbefe43f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b0b34d2e-4883-5737-85a2-37f53a7c5534" :activity/id #uuid "b0b34d2e-4883-5737-85a2-37f53a7c5534" :activity/title "Identifying Coefficients and Constants" :activity/type :activity