{:db/id "answer-field-8a3e180a-4f98-588d-a55b-f82b3f9dfac9" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a3e180a-4f98-588d-a55b-f82b3f9dfac9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-586d57ed-6322-50cd-9bf2-d3afc104c6b3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-586d57ed-6322-50cd-9bf2-d3afc104c6b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-586d57ed-6322-50cd-9bf2-d3afc104c6b3" :answer/id #uuid "586d57ed-6322-50cd-9bf2-d3afc104c6b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2175ddd7-b5c7-5bcd-b639-d4f01939487a" :question/id #uuid "2175ddd7-b5c7-5bcd-b639-d4f01939487a" :question/math-academy-id "q-180211" :question/problem "If $h=4,$ then $\\frac{3h}{2}+9=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Replacing $h$ with $4$ in the expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3h}{2}+9 & = \\\\ \\frac{3(4)}{2}+9 & = \\\\ \\frac{12}{2}+9 & = \\\\ 6+9 & = \\\\ 15 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d08a94ad-a59e-5ab7-8898-71db1e4d9b6e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d08a94ad-a59e-5ab7-8898-71db1e4d9b6e" :answer-field/id #uuid "d08a94ad-a59e-5ab7-8898-71db1e4d9b6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-baa78b79-9595-528a-8f0c-86d24b469c78" :answer-field/choices ["answer-baa78b79-9595-528a-8f0c-86d24b469c78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-baa78b79-9595-528a-8f0c-86d24b469c78" :answer/id #uuid "baa78b79-9595-528a-8f0c-86d24b469c78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a26bf3d9-e722-517d-a584-8e9fe07e450e" :question/id #uuid "a26bf3d9-e722-517d-a584-8e9fe07e450e" :question/math-academy-id "q-186031" :question/problem "Evaluate $-6a-\\frac{1}{5}$ for $a=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Replacing $a$ with $\\frac{1}{3}$ in the expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6a-\\frac{1}{5} & = \\\\ -6(\\frac{1}{3})-\\frac{1}{5} & = \\\\ -\\frac{6}{3}-\\frac{1}{5} & = \\\\ -2-\\frac{1}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{(-2)\\cdot 5-1}{5} & = \\\\ -\\frac{11}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb973e61-7d23-52e5-b2ef-12eefda53bf8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb973e61-7d23-52e5-b2ef-12eefda53bf8" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb973e61-7d23-52e5-b2ef-12eefda53bf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-41f7a202-2c88-5780-a174-3331ee2546d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41f7a202-2c88-5780-a174-3331ee2546d4" "answer-72872caa-7826-5d33-9478-418fcf7b7bc0" "answer-dc5ffa82-9e00-5078-94cf-288a2d8f398a" "answer-968707ff-2d1c-5885-9528-97f8f79a7377" "answer-5b555cc0-0ed8-506e-80ce-b3b4bdb41696"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41f7a202-2c88-5780-a174-3331ee2546d4" :answer/id #uuid "41f7a202-2c88-5780-a174-3331ee2546d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72872caa-7826-5d33-9478-418fcf7b7bc0" :answer/id #uuid "72872caa-7826-5d33-9478-418fcf7b7bc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc5ffa82-9e00-5078-94cf-288a2d8f398a" :answer/id #uuid "dc5ffa82-9e00-5078-94cf-288a2d8f398a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-968707ff-2d1c-5885-9528-97f8f79a7377" :answer/id #uuid "968707ff-2d1c-5885-9528-97f8f79a7377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b555cc0-0ed8-506e-80ce-b3b4bdb41696" :answer/id #uuid "5b555cc0-0ed8-506e-80ce-b3b4bdb41696" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9a5e0230-7894-51f3-afd6-6cc279d87228" :question/id #uuid "9a5e0230-7894-51f3-afd6-6cc279d87228" :question/math-academy-id "q-180267" :question/problem "If $y=-2,$ then $3-4(3-2y)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We replace $y$ with $-2$ in the expression and evaluate the parentheses first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-4(3-2y) & = \\\\ 3-4(3-2(-2)) & = \\\\ 3-4(3+4) & = \\\\ 3-4(7) & = \\\\ 3-28 & = \\\\ -25 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1639e847-f891-584d-90ce-1361c0620ec9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1639e847-f891-584d-90ce-1361c0620ec9" :answer-field/id #uuid "1639e847-f891-584d-90ce-1361c0620ec9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b90ecccc-4503-5760-b2d3-96866aca4524" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b90ecccc-4503-5760-b2d3-96866aca4524"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b90ecccc-4503-5760-b2d3-96866aca4524" :answer/id #uuid "b90ecccc-4503-5760-b2d3-96866aca4524" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ba0af4d-b531-5e58-b782-4b7a32460438" :question/id #uuid "3ba0af4d-b531-5e58-b782-4b7a32460438" :question/math-academy-id "q-180261" :question/problem "If $x=2,$ then $12-4(3x-4)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We replace $x$ with $2$ in the expression and evaluate the parentheses first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-4(3x-4) & = \\\\ 12-4(3\\cdot 2-4) & = \\\\ 12-4(6-4) & = \\\\ 12-4(2) & = \\\\ 12-8 & = \\\\ 4 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a444ff8-f2c0-5ca6-95a6-e2911034fd96"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a444ff8-f2c0-5ca6-95a6-e2911034fd96" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a444ff8-f2c0-5ca6-95a6-e2911034fd96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-211095ff-43cb-58b6-aefd-f9eef6c48868" :answer-field/choices ["answer-211095ff-43cb-58b6-aefd-f9eef6c48868"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-211095ff-43cb-58b6-aefd-f9eef6c48868" :answer/id #uuid "211095ff-43cb-58b6-aefd-f9eef6c48868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c819591b-7976-59a4-815e-5b13c1691fd5" :question/id #uuid "c819591b-7976-59a4-815e-5b13c1691fd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-180268" :question/problem "If $w=2$ and $z=-4,$ then $w+5z=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Replacing $w$ with $2$ and $z$ with $-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+5z & = \\\\ 2+5(-4) & = \\\\ 2-20 & = \\\\ -18 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e20507b-53cf-5029-9ff9-03e4a68206bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e20507b-53cf-5029-9ff9-03e4a68206bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e20507b-53cf-5029-9ff9-03e4a68206bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a25c3b76-33b2-5ddb-bd40-9f882ef4f25b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a25c3b76-33b2-5ddb-bd40-9f882ef4f25b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a25c3b76-33b2-5ddb-bd40-9f882ef4f25b" :answer/id #uuid "a25c3b76-33b2-5ddb-bd40-9f882ef4f25b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1eb0410f-52e0-5fe3-aa6d-2cf67e29e0a3" :question/id #uuid "1eb0410f-52e0-5fe3-aa6d-2cf67e29e0a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-180270" :question/problem "If $p=2$ and $q=-1,$ then $-p+3q=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Replacing $p$ with $2$ and $q$ with $-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-p+3q & = \\\\ -(2)+3(-1) & = \\\\ -2-3 & = \\\\ -5 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e0c1c5bf-53f5-5527-a2d2-65ab11db2807"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e0c1c5bf-53f5-5527-a2d2-65ab11db2807" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0c1c5bf-53f5-5527-a2d2-65ab11db2807" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2d52de4c-5e14-522e-ace7-29624b919a04" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d52de4c-5e14-522e-ace7-29624b919a04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d52de4c-5e14-522e-ace7-29624b919a04" :answer/id #uuid "2d52de4c-5e14-522e-ace7-29624b919a04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186056016 :tutorial/content "To **evaluate** the expression $3+x$ for $x={\\color{blue}2}$, we replace $x$ with $\\color{blue}2$ in the expression and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+x & = \\\\ 3+(2) & = \\\\ 3+2 & = \\\\ 5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186056017 :tutorial/content "The usual order of operations (PEMDAS) applies when evaluating expressions. So when an algebraic expression contains parentheses $(\\ldots)$, we calculate what's inside the parentheses *first*. \n\nFor example, we evaluate $6 - (2x+3)$ at $x=3$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-(2x+3) & = \\\\ 6-(2\\cdot 3+3) & = \\\\ 6-(6+3) & = \\\\ 6-9 & = \\\\ -3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186056018 :tutorial/content "If an expression contains more than one variable, we evaluate it using the same procedure, replacing each variable with the appropriate value.\n\nFor example, to find the value of $2b + \\dfrac{1}{2}a$ when $a=-2$ and $b=3,$ we replace $a$ with $-2$ and $b$ with $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2b+\\frac{1}{2}a & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 3+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) & = \\\\ 6-1 & = \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054916 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186122840 :answer-field/choices 17592186122843] [:db/retract 17592186122840 :answer-field/choices 17592186122844] [:db/retract 17592186122840 :answer-field/choices 17592186122845] [:db/retract 17592186122828 :answer-field/choices 17592186122832] [:db/retract 17592186122828 :answer-field/choices 17592186122833] [:db/retract 17592186122828 :answer-field/choices 17592186122829] [:db/retract 17592186122828 :answer-field/choices 17592186122830] [:db/retract 17592186122828 :answer-field/choices 17592186122831] [:db/retract 17592186124082 :answer-field/choices 17592186124083] [:db/retract 17592186124082 :answer-field/choices 17592186124084] [:db/retract 17592186124082 :answer-field/choices 17592186124085] [:db/retract 17592186124082 :answer-field/choices 17592186124086] [:db/retract 17592186124082 :answer-field/choices 17592186124087] {:db/id 17592186124594 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-824e717c-810d-5647-9a31-c9225776fabe" "question-c5298f54-bfaf-5a4f-ac68-b78b607bf15c" "question-10ac6b1a-97da-521c-a5c2-16923318bd3b" "question-d222dcc8-f398-5562-bff7-74444e587da8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124595 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-88d1b83b-2766-5063-936f-a018502be867" "question-41bc3280-6f3c-5ef7-84dc-f2df8938f974" "question-4437c604-b7f0-5633-b7e5-9971f03bd2b2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124596 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e54cb552-8c05-5b9c-84f1-978bbe7cbf63" "question-a5265619-0ee7-5042-83d2-70d3e989522b" "question-eb779ef9-c9f2-5338-9ff6-677718e082ac" "question-43a13109-9c88-5e83-9206-805f97530d84" "question-7396bdb2-9333-5e99-8459-ac9d52a00034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-824e717c-810d-5647-9a31-c9225776fabe" :question/id #uuid "824e717c-810d-5647-9a31-c9225776fabe" :question/math-academy-id "q-165280" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=2y-xy,$ find $\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta },$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta ,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and $y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂f}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2-r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =(-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,(-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )+(2-r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )+2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c55d75d-2389-5139-9713-9b0001a3628b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c55d75d-2389-5139-9713-9b0001a3628b" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c55d75d-2389-5139-9713-9b0001a3628b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d40c479d-3512-5ad6-901c-ae8cc9ca656d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d40c479d-3512-5ad6-901c-ae8cc9ca656d" "answer-6bf02a3a-6507-5e24-9dfe-fdc65427917b" "answer-cb480f73-b28d-5d1d-bf28-114396c6f5bd" "answer-ef9ed06d-7edb-5dc7-a0b5-315d2f4f833d" "answer-f4006751-8828-5338-b289-001c5c562f27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d40c479d-3512-5ad6-901c-ae8cc9ca656d" :answer/id #uuid "d40c479d-3512-5ad6-901c-ae8cc9ca656d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bf02a3a-6507-5e24-9dfe-fdc65427917b" :answer/id #uuid "6bf02a3a-6507-5e24-9dfe-fdc65427917b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb480f73-b28d-5d1d-bf28-114396c6f5bd" :answer/id #uuid "cb480f73-b28d-5d1d-bf28-114396c6f5bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef9ed06d-7edb-5dc7-a0b5-315d2f4f833d" :answer/id #uuid "ef9ed06d-7edb-5dc7-a0b5-315d2f4f833d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4006751-8828-5338-b289-001c5c562f27" :answer/id #uuid "f4006751-8828-5338-b289-001c5c562f27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125040 :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y),$ find $\\frac{∂g}{∂r},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $g(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta ,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and $y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂r}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂r} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{x+y},\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{x+y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }, \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂r} & =(\\frac{1}{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta })\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +(\\frac{1}{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta })\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{r}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186122840 :answer-field/correct 17592186122841 :answer-field/choices ["answer-19655a9a-cd78-5629-b63c-3d39429c6795" "answer-0f53b13e-3023-5aa6-80ef-b86a7b9a981e" "answer-a74e8615-6e66-546e-bfc7-29b7cec5ca41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19655a9a-cd78-5629-b63c-3d39429c6795" :answer/id #uuid "19655a9a-cd78-5629-b63c-3d39429c6795" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f53b13e-3023-5aa6-80ef-b86a7b9a981e" :answer/id #uuid "0f53b13e-3023-5aa6-80ef-b86a7b9a981e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a74e8615-6e66-546e-bfc7-29b7cec5ca41" :answer/id #uuid "a74e8615-6e66-546e-bfc7-29b7cec5ca41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c5298f54-bfaf-5a4f-ac68-b78b607bf15c" :question/id #uuid "c5298f54-bfaf-5a4f-ac68-b78b607bf15c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95115" :question/problem "Given that $h(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂h}{∂r},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $h(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta ,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and $y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂r}+\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂r} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $h$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂y}=-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂r} & =(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -(2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2r({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74be8c02-d536-5d47-b824-c1806a52210c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74be8c02-d536-5d47-b824-c1806a52210c" :answer-field/id #uuid "74be8c02-d536-5d47-b824-c1806a52210c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-194c2f16-5d03-56da-8f8a-2451146b01a1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-194c2f16-5d03-56da-8f8a-2451146b01a1" "answer-80a52cdb-4432-54c2-aba3-ba66914bcbe3" "answer-27127698-eb1f-5556-ba20-69f2d7bce69e" "answer-91e129af-e354-55a9-b266-adc2bb6d4a71" "answer-0a6d8b25-1be0-507f-9e45-600b11128f7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-194c2f16-5d03-56da-8f8a-2451146b01a1" :answer/id #uuid "194c2f16-5d03-56da-8f8a-2451146b01a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80a52cdb-4432-54c2-aba3-ba66914bcbe3" :answer/id #uuid "80a52cdb-4432-54c2-aba3-ba66914bcbe3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27127698-eb1f-5556-ba20-69f2d7bce69e" :answer/id #uuid "27127698-eb1f-5556-ba20-69f2d7bce69e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91e129af-e354-55a9-b266-adc2bb6d4a71" :answer/id #uuid "91e129af-e354-55a9-b266-adc2bb6d4a71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a6d8b25-1be0-507f-9e45-600b11128f7b" :answer/id #uuid "0a6d8b25-1be0-507f-9e45-600b11128f7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-10ac6b1a-97da-521c-a5c2-16923318bd3b" :question/id #uuid "10ac6b1a-97da-521c-a5c2-16923318bd3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95108" :question/problem "Given that $p(x,y)=2x+{y}^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂p}{∂\\theta },$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $p(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta ,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and $y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂p}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂p}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂p}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂p}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂p}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $n$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂p}{∂x}=2,\\,\\frac{∂p}{∂y}=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂p}{∂x} & =2, \\\\ \\frac{∂p}{∂y} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂p}{∂\\theta } & =-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b299f98-e7d5-5d6a-b095-d0d004a31211"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b299f98-e7d5-5d6a-b095-d0d004a31211" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b299f98-e7d5-5d6a-b095-d0d004a31211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5d8cc96a-5c3e-522a-bb6f-d8ebe3a3b80a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-860111b7-3db7-5aa8-8df9-cd797e251089" "answer-982a579f-34d1-56d7-a91d-7ee313227e85" "answer-1f6054fc-1437-5b2d-8432-34493b15c6c8" "answer-5d8cc96a-5c3e-522a-bb6f-d8ebe3a3b80a" "answer-1abaecde-f0c9-53d9-a58e-fb98f60eda2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-860111b7-3db7-5aa8-8df9-cd797e251089" :answer/id #uuid "860111b7-3db7-5aa8-8df9-cd797e251089" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-982a579f-34d1-56d7-a91d-7ee313227e85" :answer/id #uuid "982a579f-34d1-56d7-a91d-7ee313227e85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f6054fc-1437-5b2d-8432-34493b15c6c8" :answer/id #uuid "1f6054fc-1437-5b2d-8432-34493b15c6c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d8cc96a-5c3e-522a-bb6f-d8ebe3a3b80a" :answer/id #uuid "5d8cc96a-5c3e-522a-bb6f-d8ebe3a3b80a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1abaecde-f0c9-53d9-a58e-fb98f60eda2b" :answer/id #uuid "1abaecde-f0c9-53d9-a58e-fb98f60eda2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d222dcc8-f398-5562-bff7-74444e587da8" :question/id #uuid "d222dcc8-f398-5562-bff7-74444e587da8" :question/math-academy-id "q-165281" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+y,$ find $\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta },$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta ,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and $y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂f}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-549b5d38-f4aa-575f-b0f7-90b5dcfff3ea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-549b5d38-f4aa-575f-b0f7-90b5dcfff3ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "549b5d38-f4aa-575f-b0f7-90b5dcfff3ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1b6645f2-694d-5701-b91f-bf076971ef68" :answer-field/choices ["answer-53caf8ff-2acc-51ae-aaa5-97dfb713b748" "answer-dd87415c-114c-567c-b99f-b5fa2701b9a1" "answer-1b6645f2-694d-5701-b91f-bf076971ef68" "answer-64d89caa-06b3-5a99-b92b-722d4926b374" "answer-4d211281-45d7-5aac-97a5-b16e835059d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53caf8ff-2acc-51ae-aaa5-97dfb713b748" :answer/id #uuid "53caf8ff-2acc-51ae-aaa5-97dfb713b748" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+r\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd87415c-114c-567c-b99f-b5fa2701b9a1" :answer/id #uuid "dd87415c-114c-567c-b99f-b5fa2701b9a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b6645f2-694d-5701-b91f-bf076971ef68" :answer/id #uuid "1b6645f2-694d-5701-b91f-bf076971ef68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64d89caa-06b3-5a99-b92b-722d4926b374" :answer/id #uuid "64d89caa-06b3-5a99-b92b-722d4926b374" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d211281-45d7-5aac-97a5-b16e835059d2" :answer/id #uuid "4d211281-45d7-5aac-97a5-b16e835059d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125038 :question/problem "Given that $w(r,\\theta )=r(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ),$ find $\\frac{∂w}{∂y},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂w}{∂y}=\\frac{∂w}{∂r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r}=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta }=2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186122828 :answer-field/correct "answer-3a66db9c-0ec7-5bff-93d3-e61113901baa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5bacd52a-7451-5471-aa59-d1a60f4350e0" "answer-813ed5fe-e565-55ae-b0a3-dcc8c9821dc1" "answer-7bfdc48d-b632-5519-8ba3-19a0e2f15c2f" "answer-3a66db9c-0ec7-5bff-93d3-e61113901baa" "answer-3a6ab715-8c58-5119-aca6-445e2d5a78d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bacd52a-7451-5471-aa59-d1a60f4350e0" :answer/id #uuid "5bacd52a-7451-5471-aa59-d1a60f4350e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-813ed5fe-e565-55ae-b0a3-dcc8c9821dc1" :answer/id #uuid "813ed5fe-e565-55ae-b0a3-dcc8c9821dc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bfdc48d-b632-5519-8ba3-19a0e2f15c2f" :answer/id #uuid "7bfdc48d-b632-5519-8ba3-19a0e2f15c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a66db9c-0ec7-5bff-93d3-e61113901baa" :answer/id #uuid "3a66db9c-0ec7-5bff-93d3-e61113901baa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a6ab715-8c58-5119-aca6-445e2d5a78d0" :answer/id #uuid "3a6ab715-8c58-5119-aca6-445e2d5a78d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-88d1b83b-2766-5063-936f-a018502be867" :question/id #uuid "88d1b83b-2766-5063-936f-a018502be867" :question/math-academy-id "q-95137" :question/problem "Given that $h(r,\\theta )=r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1),$ find $\\frac{∂h}{∂x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂h}{∂x}=\\frac{∂h}{∂r}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $h$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂r}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta }=-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1bff08b3-d2ad-542d-9f8a-a1ea880775f8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1bff08b3-d2ad-542d-9f8a-a1ea880775f8" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bff08b3-d2ad-542d-9f8a-a1ea880775f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7368bb2b-738b-5553-9b24-d72d10f86673" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14d25be9-c593-5605-a401-5d2bd749db79" "answer-84dcc6f3-d690-5f72-8730-48a6a222d69f" "answer-7368bb2b-738b-5553-9b24-d72d10f86673" "answer-952ab814-3b74-5511-bb1b-17a92c942267" "answer-e73b53e8-31b8-587a-95b0-e9d5813a7d4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14d25be9-c593-5605-a401-5d2bd749db79" :answer/id #uuid "14d25be9-c593-5605-a401-5d2bd749db79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84dcc6f3-d690-5f72-8730-48a6a222d69f" :answer/id #uuid "84dcc6f3-d690-5f72-8730-48a6a222d69f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7368bb2b-738b-5553-9b24-d72d10f86673" :answer/id #uuid "7368bb2b-738b-5553-9b24-d72d10f86673" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-952ab814-3b74-5511-bb1b-17a92c942267" :answer/id #uuid "952ab814-3b74-5511-bb1b-17a92c942267" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e73b53e8-31b8-587a-95b0-e9d5813a7d4d" :answer/id #uuid "e73b53e8-31b8-587a-95b0-e9d5813a7d4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-41bc3280-6f3c-5ef7-84dc-f2df8938f974" :question/id #uuid "41bc3280-6f3c-5ef7-84dc-f2df8938f974" :question/math-academy-id "q-95135" :question/problem "Given that $v(r,\\theta )=r(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ),$ find $\\frac{∂v}{∂y},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂v}{∂y}=\\frac{∂v}{∂r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $v$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂r}=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }=-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a1d7bd4f-ecaa-56a0-8783-ed8687ea01ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1d7bd4f-ecaa-56a0-8783-ed8687ea01ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d7bd4f-ecaa-56a0-8783-ed8687ea01ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aa3c903d-f537-5005-92b3-162fe2194e71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e8d5bbd-e2b1-533d-9bdd-c6ed6c668040" "answer-8baa2b02-1db0-5fce-a974-ddf0773d035d" "answer-aa3c903d-f537-5005-92b3-162fe2194e71" "answer-6a2092ad-3f11-5666-b765-95bb966954f8" "answer-6c9972e3-8762-5cb3-b03e-679f5020939c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e8d5bbd-e2b1-533d-9bdd-c6ed6c668040" :answer/id #uuid "1e8d5bbd-e2b1-533d-9bdd-c6ed6c668040" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8baa2b02-1db0-5fce-a974-ddf0773d035d" :answer/id #uuid "8baa2b02-1db0-5fce-a974-ddf0773d035d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa3c903d-f537-5005-92b3-162fe2194e71" :answer/id #uuid "aa3c903d-f537-5005-92b3-162fe2194e71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a2092ad-3f11-5666-b765-95bb966954f8" :answer/id #uuid "6a2092ad-3f11-5666-b765-95bb966954f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c9972e3-8762-5cb3-b03e-679f5020939c" :answer/id #uuid "6c9972e3-8762-5cb3-b03e-679f5020939c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125247 :question/problem "Given that $v(r,\\theta )=r(2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ),$ find $\\frac{∂v}{∂x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂v}{∂x}=\\frac{∂v}{∂r}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $v$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂r}=2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }=-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =(2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124082 :answer-field/correct "answer-c7e0ff91-463d-5009-a863-3db111e986e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be832724-0d5c-5c12-8cac-57e9d7fe56e5" "answer-c7e0ff91-463d-5009-a863-3db111e986e2" "answer-cae67d8e-975c-57a3-acb6-aea452effb82" "answer-7a5455a6-a620-598c-ad7d-fe4df9304006" "answer-ed302be1-425e-5d43-9c40-6e14e1503e1f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be832724-0d5c-5c12-8cac-57e9d7fe56e5" :answer/id #uuid "be832724-0d5c-5c12-8cac-57e9d7fe56e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7e0ff91-463d-5009-a863-3db111e986e2" :answer/id #uuid "c7e0ff91-463d-5009-a863-3db111e986e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cae67d8e-975c-57a3-acb6-aea452effb82" :answer/id #uuid "cae67d8e-975c-57a3-acb6-aea452effb82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a5455a6-a620-598c-ad7d-fe4df9304006" :answer/id #uuid "7a5455a6-a620-598c-ad7d-fe4df9304006" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed302be1-425e-5d43-9c40-6e14e1503e1f" :answer/id #uuid "ed302be1-425e-5d43-9c40-6e14e1503e1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4437c604-b7f0-5633-b7e5-9971f03bd2b2" :question/id #uuid "4437c604-b7f0-5633-b7e5-9971f03bd2b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-165283" :question/problem "Given that $v(r,\\theta )={r}^{2}+2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ find $\\frac{∂v}{∂x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂v}{∂x}=\\frac{∂v}{∂r}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $v$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂r}=2r+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }=-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =(2r+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-77f83ac4-379e-5a13-8c4c-6ea313e7d773"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-77f83ac4-379e-5a13-8c4c-6ea313e7d773" :answer-field/id #uuid "77f83ac4-379e-5a13-8c4c-6ea313e7d773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-af934f8e-6b47-50f3-976d-130962164ab7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-489fb4e2-401a-51bd-8367-54c21281a25c" "answer-af934f8e-6b47-50f3-976d-130962164ab7" "answer-f8d81125-ee3b-5e23-ba6b-3f5a3fc654e1" "answer-17a74912-9939-5160-b2f2-fc9f75995b79" "answer-d704c90e-1c68-5f35-9050-f1ea9764f3d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-489fb4e2-401a-51bd-8367-54c21281a25c" :answer/id #uuid "489fb4e2-401a-51bd-8367-54c21281a25c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af934f8e-6b47-50f3-976d-130962164ab7" :answer/id #uuid "af934f8e-6b47-50f3-976d-130962164ab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8d81125-ee3b-5e23-ba6b-3f5a3fc654e1" :answer/id #uuid "f8d81125-ee3b-5e23-ba6b-3f5a3fc654e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17a74912-9939-5160-b2f2-fc9f75995b79" :answer/id #uuid "17a74912-9939-5160-b2f2-fc9f75995b79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d704c90e-1c68-5f35-9050-f1ea9764f3d9" :answer/id #uuid "d704c90e-1c68-5f35-9050-f1ea9764f3d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e54cb552-8c05-5b9c-84f1-978bbe7cbf63" :question/id #uuid "e54cb552-8c05-5b9c-84f1-978bbe7cbf63" :question/math-academy-id "q-95168" :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+{z}^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂g}{∂z},$ where $(x,y,z)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $g(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂z}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂z}+\\frac{∂g}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂g}{∂z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z}={x}^{2}+2z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z} & ={r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-45082c16-ebec-5599-aae3-e180ec356a3a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-45082c16-ebec-5599-aae3-e180ec356a3a" :answer-field/id #uuid "45082c16-ebec-5599-aae3-e180ec356a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9713ade3-5604-530d-b802-1fdfc640a4e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f69418f1-6362-5b4e-8489-03eacbf8b9bf" "answer-b62c08b7-43fb-5995-8666-a7c19ff8a830" "answer-893956da-d416-51f2-95f7-dc12fb1c1725" "answer-9713ade3-5604-530d-b802-1fdfc640a4e0" "answer-daa43c07-cab4-59d9-96d9-b09db9596eda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f69418f1-6362-5b4e-8489-03eacbf8b9bf" :answer/id #uuid "f69418f1-6362-5b4e-8489-03eacbf8b9bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +2z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b62c08b7-43fb-5995-8666-a7c19ff8a830" :answer/id #uuid "b62c08b7-43fb-5995-8666-a7c19ff8a830" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-893956da-d416-51f2-95f7-dc12fb1c1725" :answer/id #uuid "893956da-d416-51f2-95f7-dc12fb1c1725" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2rz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9713ade3-5604-530d-b802-1fdfc640a4e0" :answer/id #uuid "9713ade3-5604-530d-b802-1fdfc640a4e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-daa43c07-cab4-59d9-96d9-b09db9596eda" :answer/id #uuid "daa43c07-cab4-59d9-96d9-b09db9596eda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a5265619-0ee7-5042-83d2-70d3e989522b" :question/id #uuid "a5265619-0ee7-5042-83d2-70d3e989522b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95170" :question/problem "Given that $w(x,y,z)=x{z}^{4}+y,$ find $\\frac{∂w}{∂r},$ where $(x,y,z)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $w(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂w}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂r}+\\frac{∂w}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂r}+\\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂r} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂w}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂w}{∂y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x}={z}^{4},\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x} & ={z}^{4}, \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r} & =({z}^{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={z}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-33abe709-ff3f-57d7-b112-d74c4aa40f5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-33abe709-ff3f-57d7-b112-d74c4aa40f5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "33abe709-ff3f-57d7-b112-d74c4aa40f5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aa6caf2a-21be-526b-986f-2f7d216426b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-578fd67e-6bee-5c2b-b8bf-bcc27293593f" "answer-f4265219-f53f-5148-b2f2-d73b22c820e7" "answer-b97ad485-d546-55df-a46d-f931c8749f54" "answer-aa6caf2a-21be-526b-986f-2f7d216426b7" "answer-67ac1cbd-e9a7-5e4f-a6c5-90683547e24d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-578fd67e-6bee-5c2b-b8bf-bcc27293593f" :answer/id #uuid "578fd67e-6bee-5c2b-b8bf-bcc27293593f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4265219-f53f-5148-b2f2-d73b22c820e7" :answer/id #uuid "f4265219-f53f-5148-b2f2-d73b22c820e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{z}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b97ad485-d546-55df-a46d-f931c8749f54" :answer/id #uuid "b97ad485-d546-55df-a46d-f931c8749f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa6caf2a-21be-526b-986f-2f7d216426b7" :answer/id #uuid "aa6caf2a-21be-526b-986f-2f7d216426b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67ac1cbd-e9a7-5e4f-a6c5-90683547e24d" :answer/id #uuid "67ac1cbd-e9a7-5e4f-a6c5-90683547e24d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-eb779ef9-c9f2-5338-9ff6-677718e082ac" :question/id #uuid "eb779ef9-c9f2-5338-9ff6-677718e082ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-95169" :question/problem "Given that $h(x,y,z)=xyz,$ find $\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta },$ where $(x,y,z)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $h(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂h}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂h}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂h}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $h$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x}=yz,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂y}=xz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =rz\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta } & =-(rz\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-{r}^{2}z{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}z({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={r}^{2}z\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce5f4636-c6b9-5bae-8b55-2a495ce5b39c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce5f4636-c6b9-5bae-8b55-2a495ce5b39c" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce5f4636-c6b9-5bae-8b55-2a495ce5b39c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-188706c6-3a9a-59e2-a321-b5f7df7e0d47" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48daba33-40ff-5944-964d-6c1da24ee2b1" "answer-b483533f-bf6d-5af3-85eb-651c6a343298" "answer-bfd84997-1bc6-5e77-af1c-2104ef3b0bee" "answer-188706c6-3a9a-59e2-a321-b5f7df7e0d47" "answer-cb23270c-5341-5bc3-a497-83e69396e2b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48daba33-40ff-5944-964d-6c1da24ee2b1" :answer/id #uuid "48daba33-40ff-5944-964d-6c1da24ee2b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b483533f-bf6d-5af3-85eb-651c6a343298" :answer/id #uuid "b483533f-bf6d-5af3-85eb-651c6a343298" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "rz{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfd84997-1bc6-5e77-af1c-2104ef3b0bee" :answer/id #uuid "bfd84997-1bc6-5e77-af1c-2104ef3b0bee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-188706c6-3a9a-59e2-a321-b5f7df7e0d47" :answer/id #uuid "188706c6-3a9a-59e2-a321-b5f7df7e0d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}z\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb23270c-5341-5bc3-a497-83e69396e2b6" :answer/id #uuid "cb23270c-5341-5bc3-a497-83e69396e2b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-43a13109-9c88-5e83-9206-805f97530d84" :question/id #uuid "43a13109-9c88-5e83-9206-805f97530d84" :question/math-academy-id "q-95045" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{3}+{z}^{4},$ find $\\frac{∂f}{∂r},$ where $(x,y,z)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $f(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂r}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂r}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂r} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =3{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂r} & =(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +(3{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2r{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +3{r}^{2}{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dbfbb460-7f02-5f92-88f0-57dd4c8eadf2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbfbb460-7f02-5f92-88f0-57dd4c8eadf2" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbfbb460-7f02-5f92-88f0-57dd4c8eadf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1506c3d3-af67-5f60-9fbf-f85df4c42324" :answer-field/choices ["answer-61401e41-69fe-5937-b2e0-2a0aea6f6035" "answer-b9805fe1-fc17-516a-93d3-42522d950906" "answer-d46accdd-6789-5230-a789-5a2c14364ec2" "answer-1506c3d3-af67-5f60-9fbf-f85df4c42324" "answer-01f1b62c-f9ad-5062-b0e1-04d51f193f31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61401e41-69fe-5937-b2e0-2a0aea6f6035" :answer/id #uuid "61401e41-69fe-5937-b2e0-2a0aea6f6035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+3{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9805fe1-fc17-516a-93d3-42522d950906" :answer/id #uuid "b9805fe1-fc17-516a-93d3-42522d950906" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{4}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d46accdd-6789-5230-a789-5a2c14364ec2" :answer/id #uuid "d46accdd-6789-5230-a789-5a2c14364ec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{r}^{3}{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1506c3d3-af67-5f60-9fbf-f85df4c42324" :answer/id #uuid "1506c3d3-af67-5f60-9fbf-f85df4c42324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +3{r}^{2}{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01f1b62c-f9ad-5062-b0e1-04d51f193f31" :answer/id #uuid "01f1b62c-f9ad-5062-b0e1-04d51f193f31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{3}{sin}^{4}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7396bdb2-9333-5e99-8459-ac9d52a00034" :question/id #uuid "7396bdb2-9333-5e99-8459-ac9d52a00034" :question/math-academy-id "q-165285" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂f}{∂z},$ where $(x,y,z)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $f(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂z}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂z}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂f}{∂z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2xyz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =2{r}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-52931c2c-52e1-5448-b25c-5e4f502aa192"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-52931c2c-52e1-5448-b25c-5e4f502aa192" :answer-field/id #uuid "52931c2c-52e1-5448-b25c-5e4f502aa192" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0466a8b0-0e72-50a8-9e40-0c1214a8a281" :answer-field/choices ["answer-074a0854-45c8-5e8e-88a6-4963ee2622c9" "answer-d4935e49-5ceb-5de5-a639-1d44e14dc969" "answer-aa1073de-8640-5caf-b844-a33c80d8ae74" "answer-0466a8b0-0e72-50a8-9e40-0c1214a8a281" "answer-1a085611-6858-54c9-855d-19621bc6a77a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-074a0854-45c8-5e8e-88a6-4963ee2622c9" :answer/id #uuid "074a0854-45c8-5e8e-88a6-4963ee2622c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2rz\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4935e49-5ceb-5de5-a639-1d44e14dc969" :answer/id #uuid "d4935e49-5ceb-5de5-a639-1d44e14dc969" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "rz\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa1073de-8640-5caf-b844-a33c80d8ae74" :answer/id #uuid "aa1073de-8640-5caf-b844-a33c80d8ae74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0466a8b0-0e72-50a8-9e40-0c1214a8a281" :answer/id #uuid "0466a8b0-0e72-50a8-9e40-0c1214a8a281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a085611-6858-54c9-855d-19621bc6a77a" :answer/id #uuid "1a085611-6858-54c9-855d-19621bc6a77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125837 :tutorial/content "Given a function $f(x,y),$ how do we calculate the partial derivatives $f_r$ and $f_\\theta,$ where $(r,\\theta)$ are plane polar coordinates?\n\nTo do this, we can use the multivariable chain rule. First, let's write down our tree diagram.\n\n![](images/7f/7f19c4a682b30f1eea1d9c1be7da83bd77ba137173f25eb9c7e5cf253abba015.png)\n\nFrom the tree diagram, we can see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂r}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂r} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's take the partial derivatives of $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂r} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  &  &  & \\frac{∂y}{∂r} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta } & =-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  &  &  & \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta } & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these results into the multivariable chain rule, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =-\\frac{∂f}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125847 :tutorial/content "Up to now, we've been using the following formulas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{r} & ={f}_{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{f}_{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {f}_{\\theta } & =-r{f}_{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +r{f}_{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can treat the above as a system of equations in the \"unknowns\" $f_x$ and $f_y.$ Solving this system gives explicit expressions for $f_x$ and $f_y$ in terms of functions of $r$ and $\\theta.$\n\nFor example, suppose we want an explicit formula for $f_x.$ We can eliminate $f_y$ by multiplying the first equation by $r\\cos\\theta$ and the second equation by $\\sin\\theta$ to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r{f}_{r}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =r{f}_{x}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +r{f}_{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ {f}_{\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =-r{f}_{x}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +r{f}_{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first gives\n\n$$\nr f_r \\cos\\theta - f_\\theta \\sin\\theta = r f_x(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta),\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\nf_x = f_r \\cos\\theta - \\dfrac1r f_\\theta \\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can use a similar procedure to write $f_y$ in terms of functions of $r$ and $\\theta.$ Our results as summarized below:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial x} &= \\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial r} \\cos \\theta\n\t\t\t\t\t\t-\\dfrac{1}{r} \\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial \\theta}\\sin \\theta\\[1ex]\n\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial y} &= \\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial r} \\sin \\theta\n\t\t\t\t\t\t+ \\dfrac{1}{r} \\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial \\theta}\\cos \\theta\n}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125838 :tutorial/content "Given a function of three variables $f(x,y,z),$ we can find formulas for $f_r, f_\\theta,$ and $f_z,$ where $(r,\\theta,z)$ are cylindrical polar coordinates. The results that we need are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =-\\frac{∂f}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the first and second equations are identical to the equations derived for plane polar coordinates, as we would expect. \n\nThe difference here is that we now have a third equation that deals with the $z$-dependence. But since the $z$-coordinate is the same in both Cartesian and cylindrical polar coordinates, we can simply differentiate with respect to $z$ as usual.\n\nLet's see an example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125848 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we have a function $f(x,y,z),$ and we wish to find formulas for $f_\\rho,$ $f_\\theta,$ and $f_\\phi$, where $(\\rho,\\theta,\\phi)$ are spherical polar coordinates.\n\nUsing the multivariable chain rule, it can be shown that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\rho } & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =-\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂ϕ} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nYou might want to try deriving these formulas for yourself!" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124734 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fb1f16a0-3031-5b97-a1fa-27b860c24df9" "question-88def0e2-16e4-59a7-96bb-d850c4ea1c49" "question-084c02e4-7974-5581-92ae-668d0f97c0f4" "question-501022bc-dca6-55f9-9b78-5c4a339dd1a1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119706 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n\n![](images/9d/9d0b186213211813b290f502888f68e0603bc9f77bcd7ea9d6262cb7449c00e7.svg)\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/42/4298fe244fd6c66c7623ad508c97b96464321387506aa1e4be5e2399a5c9a862.svg)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 66\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ 15{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=5$ and $y_2=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, ![](images/a8/a86dfd0e07b8c415e526764cf9f7ba8f020609bf7b13cc90536deba868ec4aa6.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e717653a-60c8-527b-b3b4-e108ff685e10" "question-7099a838-c9d8-54d6-9fec-92d9fefe3598" "question-53971d39-ffaa-5c20-9081-d54743d61b0a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119611 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n![](images/a1/a13a7752a224bdabc27558a6a41e2b24d3c7918af1ca4d9cff802dcb54259238.svg)\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/60/605f569e0b4a54d2ca68d7b3330a2a0ebb06dcaba2b7efa911f58dbffd796fb0.svg)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n![](images/d2/d259a6740aa32e0e577756375fd85589b815232314511c74dc434a88d0146a3b.svg)\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4 \\\\ {y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =4-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =4-(2) \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1-(2)+2(2) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/c5/c5198aa83d3976d992b200f63941261f952282fedb241db780c20c12c97e3ba9.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9ad4c6c3-50cf-5ba9-ae9f-35f5ce660c90" "question-ab64b08c-fec6-5dff-b1cc-ff3d1f5e73c7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119610 :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ given by\n![](images/f1/f1124e83e3b7614557a1a6de54523cc99f62ba2a52af1da8e4d22e14466ce020.svg)\nIf $\\langle x_1,x_2 \\rangle$ and $\\langle y_1,y_2 \\rangle$ are the solutions to the systems $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $L\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{b}$ respectively, what is the value of $x_1 \\cdot y_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/a1/a185a6fd91c78ed3e291b3ac8b99f9430290e5d8c1060a7d97317efc230aeb40.svg)\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/1e/1e780d384ca1fd957d742bbd047399c558ab016d187ce4cf71682546673aba35.svg)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=6$ and $y_2=4.$ Therefore, \n![](images/58/58da62903247cf6dfdf33be86293c181ef5184048ca7cd6c921360e5d202f353.svg)\n\n- Next, we solve $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/e0/e0563dde4944ecbe2ccb98bc91246fa18c7a808df96ab77f9f8efb5510084677.svg)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $x_2=-2$ and $x_1=2.$ Therefore, \n![](images/a8/a84088cff2a3589652ef7cabf09e3d8429fad7797ea20d44a416f85dcc7f9b65.svg)\n\nFinally, $x_1 \\cdot y_2 = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241124 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=7 \\\\ -10{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=7$ and ${y}_{2}=34.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}].$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb1f16a0-3031-5b97-a1fa-27b860c24df9" :question/id #uuid "fb1f16a0-3031-5b97-a1fa-27b860c24df9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105753" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=9 \\\\ 11{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=9$ and ${y}_{2}=-49.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -49\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-db587132-2223-5d73-bd8b-93dbc82d6d91"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db587132-2223-5d73-bd8b-93dbc82d6d91" :answer-field/id #uuid "db587132-2223-5d73-bd8b-93dbc82d6d91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9043cde5-3c71-5771-9a3d-347775e2a488" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa9afe1b-bb2b-5925-8cb5-cfde20011076" "answer-81b0d9a3-f05e-52aa-baca-6aa189c65731" "answer-9043cde5-3c71-5771-9a3d-347775e2a488" "answer-1c72a1a6-e9cc-5dc7-8129-ca02b99a9f47" "answer-204b0962-b138-56df-b0fd-2796efaabbe5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa9afe1b-bb2b-5925-8cb5-cfde20011076" :answer/id #uuid "fa9afe1b-bb2b-5925-8cb5-cfde20011076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81b0d9a3-f05e-52aa-baca-