nd{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-2 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-2$ and ${y}_{2}=5.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53bb28f7-eb24-5527-b2b9-b9e6a0b7f670"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53bb28f7-eb24-5527-b2b9-b9e6a0b7f670" :answer-field/id #uuid "53bb28f7-eb24-5527-b2b9-b9e6a0b7f670" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a20766a5-d1e0-5ad7-86ef-477529985f26" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7f0c9743-f8c0-561f-ab43-b3ac76dffb0b" "answer-22731b55-f78a-5a55-92f4-008ff3141486" "answer-a20766a5-d1e0-5ad7-86ef-477529985f26" "answer-f8caf96d-5269-56da-a649-68d0844a6110" "answer-9e5361cb-8aa1-5d87-98cb-cd1a2de8325f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f0c9743-f8c0-561f-ab43-b3ac76dffb0b" :answer/id #uuid "7f0c9743-f8c0-561f-ab43-b3ac76dffb0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22731b55-f78a-5a55-92f4-008ff3141486" :answer/id #uuid "22731b55-f78a-5a55-92f4-008ff3141486" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a20766a5-d1e0-5ad7-86ef-477529985f26" :answer/id #uuid "a20766a5-d1e0-5ad7-86ef-477529985f26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8caf96d-5269-56da-a649-68d0844a6110" :answer/id #uuid "f8caf96d-5269-56da-a649-68d0844a6110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e5361cb-8aa1-5d87-98cb-cd1a2de8325f" :answer/id #uuid "9e5361cb-8aa1-5d87-98cb-cd1a2de8325f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241145 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=9 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=7 \\\\ -9{y}_{1}+{y}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =9, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =7-7{y}_{1} \\\\  & =7-7(9) \\\\  & =-56, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-1+9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+9(9) \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}].$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186377100 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =1, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+2(1) \\\\  & =0, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =2+{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2+(1)-(0) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-e717653a-60c8-527b-b3b4-e108ff685e10" :question/id #uuid "e717653a-60c8-527b-b3b4-e108ff685e10" :question/math-academy-id "q-105932" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =3, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =1-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =1-(3) \\\\  & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-3-2{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-3-2(3)+2(-2) \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6844dfb-a5ce-580b-b6b3-0beb630d472c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6844dfb-a5ce-580b-b6b3-0beb630d472c" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6844dfb-a5ce-580b-b6b3-0beb630d472c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a10292bf-b579-5963-ba7f-90d1ac0490d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e2d06e1-3417-5d35-8cf9-65a546979702" "answer-79133504-cdc8-50d1-aa34-0969c29bcf2b" "answer-a10292bf-b579-5963-ba7f-90d1ac0490d4" "answer-8fd1c199-45e5-5ea6-978f-4358accf0c0c" "answer-956543c5-8ef1-5bc5-846f-2b5c75aeb0b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e2d06e1-3417-5d35-8cf9-65a546979702" :answer/id #uuid "5e2d06e1-3417-5d35-8cf9-65a546979702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79133504-cdc8-50d1-aa34-0969c29bcf2b" :answer/id #uuid "79133504-cdc8-50d1-aa34-0969c29bcf2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a10292bf-b579-5963-ba7f-90d1ac0490d4" :answer/id #uuid "a10292bf-b579-5963-ba7f-90d1ac0490d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fd1c199-45e5-5ea6-978f-4358accf0c0c" :answer/id #uuid "8fd1c199-45e5-5ea6-978f-4358accf0c0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-956543c5-8ef1-5bc5-846f-2b5c75aeb0b1" :answer/id #uuid "956543c5-8ef1-5bc5-846f-2b5c75aeb0b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7099a838-c9d8-54d6-9fec-92d9fefe3598" :question/id #uuid "7099a838-c9d8-54d6-9fec-92d9fefe3598" :question/math-academy-id "q-107184" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}-3{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-4, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-5-2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-5-2(-4) \\\\  & =3, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =9+4{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2} \\\\  & =9+4(-4)+3(3) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-48192aeb-3b0f-5497-bc1d-dd799e8a5dc9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-48192aeb-3b0f-5497-bc1d-dd799e8a5dc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "48192aeb-3b0f-5497-bc1d-dd799e8a5dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2e232736-d49a-5bd9-b675-ee5259fec02e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-95cf673a-2ed5-5f8f-8bf1-3f41b9554c32" "answer-aadef4be-b14a-56bf-bbcb-88222c60c6ba" "answer-a4e2561d-5010-5edc-889a-d78a29403e9e" "answer-2e232736-d49a-5bd9-b675-ee5259fec02e" "answer-815e68e7-ca75-58f1-bcfc-ed2da4282e27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95cf673a-2ed5-5f8f-8bf1-3f41b9554c32" :answer/id #uuid "95cf673a-2ed5-5f8f-8bf1-3f41b9554c32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aadef4be-b14a-56bf-bbcb-88222c60c6ba" :answer/id #uuid "aadef4be-b14a-56bf-bbcb-88222c60c6ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4e2561d-5010-5edc-889a-d78a29403e9e" :answer/id #uuid "a4e2561d-5010-5edc-889a-d78a29403e9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e232736-d49a-5bd9-b675-ee5259fec02e" :answer/id #uuid "2e232736-d49a-5bd9-b675-ee5259fec02e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-815e68e7-ca75-58f1-bcfc-ed2da4282e27" :answer/id #uuid "815e68e7-ca75-58f1-bcfc-ed2da4282e27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-53971d39-ffaa-5c20-9081-d54743d61b0a" :question/id #uuid "53971d39-ffaa-5c20-9081-d54743d61b0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-32579" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2 \\\\ {y}_{1}-{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =6, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-(6)+4 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9d96da9c-3e97-52fd-92c9-c73ab85d4165"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d96da9c-3e97-52fd-92c9-c73ab85d4165" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d96da9c-3e97-52fd-92c9-c73ab85d4165" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a28f92ee-2682-564b-832c-3e2a4ecbc8c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3aea1048-26e5-56d0-bd6c-955510f59840" "answer-1c178bab-1c92-5a25-ae64-df6277ac397a" "answer-067598d2-ade2-5dd5-8073-c389ff24174b" "answer-81992826-cc58-58c1-a7a5-01d46348c63f" "answer-a28f92ee-2682-564b-832c-3e2a4ecbc8c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3aea1048-26e5-56d0-bd6c-955510f59840" :answer/id #uuid "3aea1048-26e5-56d0-bd6c-955510f59840" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c178bab-1c92-5a25-ae64-df6277ac397a" :answer/id #uuid "1c178bab-1c92-5a25-ae64-df6277ac397a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-067598d2-ade2-5dd5-8073-c389ff24174b" :answer/id #uuid "067598d2-ade2-5dd5-8073-c389ff24174b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81992826-cc58-58c1-a7a5-01d46348c63f" :answer/id #uuid "81992826-cc58-58c1-a7a5-01d46348c63f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a28f92ee-2682-564b-832c-3e2a4ecbc8c1" :answer/id #uuid "a28f92ee-2682-564b-832c-3e2a4ecbc8c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ad4c6c3-50cf-5ba9-ae9f-35f5ce660c90" :question/id #uuid "9ad4c6c3-50cf-5ba9-ae9f-35f5ce660c90" :question/math-academy-id "q-107497" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=1 \\\\ 9{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=1$ and ${y}_{2}=-3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 6{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{1}=(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot 1=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5d527114-1572-54ac-b766-1707893768e2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d527114-1572-54ac-b766-1707893768e2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d527114-1572-54ac-b766-1707893768e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fcc58994-bee3-54d3-8345-6cff06c3be4f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d358ce26-83c5-527a-b35c-94335a5980f8" "answer-fcc58994-bee3-54d3-8345-6cff06c3be4f" "answer-a0981e4f-9bc7-5c90-b871-88aafbf5dc4b" "answer-6ed5ec33-0fac-5b1f-8846-71b9668a161a" "answer-0dc9a6bd-a591-5999-b245-91b38db136b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d358ce26-83c5-527a-b35c-94335a5980f8" :answer/id #uuid "d358ce26-83c5-527a-b35c-94335a5980f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcc58994-bee3-54d3-8345-6cff06c3be4f" :answer/id #uuid "fcc58994-bee3-54d3-8345-6cff06c3be4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0981e4f-9bc7-5c90-b871-88aafbf5dc4b" :answer/id #uuid "a0981e4f-9bc7-5c90-b871-88aafbf5dc4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ed5ec33-0fac-5b1f-8846-71b9668a161a" :answer/id #uuid "6ed5ec33-0fac-5b1f-8846-71b9668a161a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0dc9a6bd-a591-5999-b245-91b38db136b1" :answer/id #uuid "0dc9a6bd-a591-5999-b245-91b38db136b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186390757 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=3$ and ${y}_{2}=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 3=-\\frac{9}{2}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ab64b08c-fec6-5dff-b1cc-ff3d1f5e73c7" :question/id #uuid "ab64b08c-fec6-5dff-b1cc-ff3d1f5e73c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32566" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of $\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=3$ and ${y}_{2}=-12.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-12$ and ${x}_{1}=-5.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d05942a2-78c5-5b8e-b7fc-65092edacbc2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d05942a2-78c5-5b8e-b7fc-65092edacbc2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d05942a2-78c5-5b8e-b7fc-65092edacbc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-521a4a18-d5e1-5275-86bd-fd4d0bbb7613" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4a94ece-2daa-5c37-8ecc-a6ffaebd161a" "answer-521a4a18-d5e1-5275-86bd-fd4d0bbb7613" "answer-9126f568-e746-57ed-bb73-ef7602c0d19e" "answer-1f0224fe-d8c2-5cc1-8f3c-e522430032e7" "answer-49b907b6-2183-5755-bb06-f22146e37570"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4a94ece-2daa-5c37-8ecc-a6ffaebd161a" :answer/id #uuid "c4a94ece-2daa-5c37-8ecc-a6ffaebd161a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-521a4a18-d5e1-5275-86bd-fd4d0bbb7613" :answer/id #uuid "521a4a18-d5e1-5275-86bd-fd4d0bbb7613" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9126f568-e746-57ed-bb73-ef7602c0d19e" :answer/id #uuid "9126f568-e746-57ed-bb73-ef7602c0d19e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f0224fe-d8c2-5cc1-8f3c-e522430032e7" :answer/id #uuid "1f0224fe-d8c2-5cc1-8f3c-e522430032e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{134}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49b907b6-2183-5755-bb06-f22146e37570" :answer/id #uuid "49b907b6-2183-5755-bb06-f22146e37570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{188}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186302218 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-4$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-4+3(-\\frac{2}{3})=-6.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241147 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=14.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-7$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{26}{7}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{26}{7} \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=\\frac{26}{7}\\cdot 14=52.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121031 :tutorial/content "There is an algorithm that uses $LU$ factorization to solve systems of equations of the form \n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b} .\n$$\n\nFor example, let's solve the following equation:\n\n![](images/77/77bbf7683a8ecfbd6864ce82eede96dcab60480e9f5395ac38eae88218af8fde.svg)\n\nSince the LU factorization of $A$ is\n\n![](images/d7/d704b00f3e25fdd85fcf123baf0340f87b82125ae2ce0718891102c9da9968f2.svg)\nour equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ can be written as\n\n![](images/14/1481be73064ba910f27931cba3f6a252123090c055ed3d4eb3657fd9b9084c58.svg)\n\ni.e., \n\n$$\nLU\\mathbf{x}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nNow, suppose we set $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ Substituting this into the above, we have\n\n$$\nL\\mathbf{y}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nIn other words, we can reduce the problem to the following system of matrix equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $L$ and $U$ are both triangular, each of these equations is easily solvable using back and forward substitution.\n\n- First, we solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Let's assume that ![](images/46/46e89549c82a3571050bf103d9f539cfd82c197c6c0ffef9161ed3c67cdbb4c0.svg) Then, we have\n![](images/af/af1f7463d07d4ddf3f25b8ae1cff3d658f8c0d2a9ab8295c5ea1e0e9c69d2fe6.svg)\nwhich gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-1 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation using *forward* substitution, we get the solution\n![](images/5b/5bb589d79fbb718f91b5df14ae4c7ac0a3767cb625c2079c0b16562b74484491.svg)\n\n- Finally, we solve $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ We have\n![](images/4a/4a54f9bbd8830b3be687a168c8d9548466124669f8e7309ee18e1f05904fd084.svg)\nwhich gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation using *back* substitution, we get the solution\n![](images/ba/baf88432261a561613c0241b2d768e9cedf4f4eddaecaaf761b774c36c1ed541.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120004 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
